= 13 October 2023 — Innovation arrives with an election-day timestamp

NIK reports that NCBR's **Fast Track — Digital Innovations** competition did
not follow its own rules or the statutory requirements of transparent,
impartial selection. Of 434 applications seeking more than **PLN 3 billion**,
117 projects were initially recommended for more than **PLN 801 million**.
Payments were stopped after press reports and ministerial review removed
projects from the list; recommendation is not proof that every złoty was paid.

The audit nevertheless finds political influence, an opaque selection of
experts and instructions from the director to assess part of project budgets
more liberally. One proposed grant of nearly PLN 123 million exceeded the
applicable limit; another for nearly PLN 55 million survived a defective
evaluation before being removed. NIK announces referrals to prosecutors,
OLAF and the Commission while NCBR is due to help administer roughly **PLN 36
billion** in the next innovation programme.

[? if nik_referral_channel = 1: The NIK channel built in 2019–20 is still
open. We can demand documents from the institution that already has them,
instead of discovering audit independence thirteen days before an election.?]
[? if nik_referral_channel = 0: We gave up our practical NIK channel years
ago. The loudest scandal of election week has arrived with an evidence route
we cannot credibly claim as our own.?]

- @ncbr_expert_register
- @ncbr_audit_file
- @ncbr_election_attack

