Every ranking change, expert instruction and disputed limit is indexed once
and delivered to institutions with different powers. Lewica refuses to call
every applicant corrupt and refuses to let institutional overlap turn into a
reason nobody owns the file.

The finding will mature after the election. That is a poor clip and a durable
problem for every person whose signature appears in the annex.

- @poland_event_queue: File the joined dossier

@ncbr_election_attack
title: Put the PLN 55 million application on every election-night screen
subtitle: The tastiest immediate swing. Turn an institutional audit into one unforgettable grant number and accept what disappears outside the frame.
on-arrival: ncbr_response = "Election-week grant attack"; media_capacity += 5; left_poll_momentum += 0.7; pis_poll_momentum -= 0.75; konf_poll_momentum += 0.1; science_grant_scrutiny -= 3; public_trust -= 2; institutional_trust -= 2; public_mood_pending_rule_of_law_backlash += 7; public_mood_pending_rule_of_law_left_ownership += 3; news_headline = "PLN 55 million becomes the final grant number of the election campaign"

The number is repeated until the institution disappears behind it. PiS spends
the final campaign hours defending a selection process that NIK itself found
defective, and Lewica receives exactly the movement the graphic was built to
produce.

The fact that the application was removed before a contract was signed becomes
a footnote. So do the expert panels, future PLN 36 billion programme and the
rules needed to stop a repeat. The attack is potent because it is narrower
than the audit.

- @poland_event_queue: Run the grant number

