= 31 March 2025 — The dashboard is not a laboratory

The Supreme Audit Office has examined the **Łukasiewicz Research Network**.
More than **PLN 2.8 billion** in state funding passed through the network from
2019 to the middle of 2024, but no approved four- or ten-year strategy says
what that money was meant to achieve. The management dashboard cannot reliably
identify which institute ran a project, what it cost or whether it finished.
One 2022 report counted 1,113 projects worth PLN 5.7 billion; the underlying
dashboard supplied different counts and included office-document systems and
an archive humidity meter among research-and-development work.

The audit follows the science ministry's July 2024 internal review. That review
reported missing work products, a missing central contract register and
additional management benefits estimated at **PLN 8.4 million**, then sent a
notification to prosecutors. A notification is not a conviction, and the NIK
finding is broader than one criminal file: for five years the state financed a
research network without retaining the information needed to judge it.

[? if left_in_government = 1: This cabinet appointed the new management and
published the review. It can claim the discovery only if it also accepts the
repair bill.?][? if left_in_government = 0: From opposition, Lewica can demand
the records without having to explain why the ministry has not yet produced
them.?]

[? if lukasiewicz_audit_prepared = 1: The grant trail built after NCBR and
Willa Plus already has the fields this network omitted. A choice made in the
last parliament now removes both an excuse and most of the setup cost.?]
[? if lukasiewicz_audit_prepared = 0: NCBR, Willa Plus and now Łukasiewicz
have each arrived as a separate scandal because we never forced their grants,
contracts and results onto one reusable record.?]

- @lukasiewicz_ledger
- @lukasiewicz_laboratories
- @lukasiewicz_partisan

