Project, institute, budget, commercial partner, status and result: one ledger,
using one definition. Contracts are published beside the work product or the
legal reason it cannot be. NIK retains access to the source records rather than
receiving another presentation exported from the same dashboard.

Researchers acquire an irritating reporting duty. Management loses the ability
to count a humidity meter differently according to the audience. For the first
time, failure and useful applied research can be distinguished without a party
spokesperson standing between them.

- @poland_event_queue: Open the ledger

@lukasiewicz_laboratories
title: Protect researchers' pay while replacing the centre's management rules
subtitle: Keep the institutes and their public mission; cut executive extras, standardise contracts and put the recovered money into laboratory staff.
on-arrival: public_sector_support += 4; labor_credibility += 4; administrative_reform_pressure += 4; public_trust += 3; left_poll_momentum += 0.3; pis_poll_momentum -= 0.1; public_mood_pending_social_spending_support += 3; public_mood_pending_social_spending_left_ownership += 5; news_headline = "The Łukasiewicz repair protects laboratories and cuts management privileges"

Lewica refuses the convenient conclusion that a badly governed public network
proves public research should not exist. Standard contracts replace bespoke
executive clauses, the centre loses posts it cannot justify, and institute
staff publish what the recovered money buys in laboratories and wages.

Managers call it a purge. Market liberals call it protection of a failed
structure. Researchers who were asked to deliver applied science near the
minimum wage finally hear a scandal response addressed to somebody below the
executive floor.

- @poland_event_queue: Send the rules to every institute

@lukasiewicz_partisan
title: Brand every discrepancy as PiS science patronage
subtitle: The sharpest immediate poll hit; it collapses a system audit into a campaign charge before every allegation has been tested.
on-arrival: media_capacity += 4; left_poll_momentum += 0.5; pis_poll_momentum -= 0.55; party_finance_scandal += 3; public_trust -= 1; institutional_trust -= 2; public_mood_pending_rule_of_law_backlash += 7; public_mood_pending_rule_of_law_left_ownership += 2; news_headline = "Łukasiewicz becomes a national indictment of PiS patronage"

The project counts, lost records and management clauses are placed beneath one
party logo. The attack lands because PiS created the network and ran the state
when the records were made. It also outruns the evidence: administrative
failure, poor metrics and every disputed contract become one corruption case
before prosecutors or auditors have said that they are.

The poll movement is immediate. The institutional repair is not. Whoever next
publishes an exculpatory document will describe the whole audit as a campaign
operation, and will have this speech to prove the point.

- @poland_event_queue: Run the indictment

