= 15 April 2025 — The synergy was future; the discount was immediate

NIK concludes that assets sold as remedies for the Orlen–Lotos merger went for
at least **PLN 5 billion below** its valuation. Orlen's own estimate puts the
gap near PLN 4 billion. NIK says the sale price was roughly half its valuation
and calls the disposal uneconomic; it also describes Orlen's projected **PLN
10.7 billion** of synergies through 2032 as illustrative and uncertain.

The audit is more than a valuation quarrel. Aramco obtained rights over half
the products of the Gdańsk refinery and vetoes over strategic decisions. NIK
says the Treasury lost influence over about 20% of Polish-refined products and
that promised petrochemical and R&D cooperation had not materialised. Orlen
can contest the audit's assumptions; it cannot make the ownership rights
disappear by changing the spreadsheet.

[? if state_company_governance_pressure >= 10: In September 2023 we attacked
the governance mechanism behind Orlen's election fuel price. The later audit
has delivered a much larger number through the same boardroom door.?]
[? if state_company_governance_pressure < 10: We enjoyed or denounced the 2023
pump price without building a durable state-company rule. The receipt is now
PLN 5 billion and somebody else wrote it.?]
[? if nik_referral_channel = 1: Our long NIK relationship gives us the audit
trail and the institutional risk.?][? if nik_referral_channel = 0: We have the
headline but no prior claim on the audit machinery that produced it.?]

- @lotos_governance
- @lotos_security
- @lotos_half_price

