= 19 September 2025 — Recovery and resilience, now with cup holders

A month earlier, media users opened the KPO beneficiary map and found HoReCa
diversification projects involving boats, floating saunas, spas and equipment
whose social purpose is difficult to explain in one screenshot. The programme
was designed to help pandemic-hit hospitality, tourism and culture businesses
add new services; the political image is a recovery fund buying toys for
owners.

The ministry froze further payments until contracts passed control. At the
19 September checkpoint, all **3,206** projects have been screened, 1,389 are
selected for deeper review, and the first 39 completed controls find seven
irregularities. One of three deeply checked watercraft projects is noncompliant;
other photogenic or politically connected projects prove compliant at that
stage. Outrage is a lead, not an audit result.

[? if horeca_kpo_prepared = 1: Earlier KPO choices produced both delivery and
a scrutiny trail. The coalition takes damage, but it can identify contracts
without stopping the whole recovery plan.?]
[? if horeca_kpo_prepared = 0: We built announcements faster than controls.
Every yacht picture now stands in for the KPO ledger the player declined to
make legible.?]
[? if left_in_government = 1: This is our coalition's control failure even
where a scheme began under PiS. Opposition parties need only decide which
luxury noun to repeat.?][? if left_in_government = 0: We own none of the
contracts and all of the screenshots, unless we choose to defend a recovery
programme whose beneficiaries are not all guilty.?]

