Every frozen contract receives a reason: conflict risk, business-plan mismatch,
missing service or pricing anomaly. A compliant sauna is politically ridiculous
and legally payable; a boat not offered to customers is neither. The distinction
is published before money resumes.

With the earlier ledger, the ministry isolates risk. Without it, officials
rebuild the evidence while a KPO deadline keeps moving.

