= January 2026 — A twenty-five-year negotiation reaches the tractor line

On 9 January the Council authorises the EU–Mercosur agreements over Poland's
opposition. On 17 January the Union and Argentina, Brazil, Paraguay and Uruguay
sign them in Asunción. The interim trade agreement can remove tariffs without
waiting for every national parliament; the wider partnership still needs the
longer ratification route.

There are real gains outside agriculture: new markets, cheaper inputs and less
dependence on a narrower set of trading partners. There is also concentrated
risk. Beef, poultry, sugar, ethanol, rice, honey and maize enter the safeguard
ledger because a price fall or import surge can land in one county long before
an export gain appears in national GDP. The accelerated safeguard mechanism
can open an investigation after a five-percent disturbance and use provisional
measures in an emergency. Farmers ask who absorbs the loss while Brussels
investigates.

The argument is no niche grievance. A January CBOS survey finds only **16%** in
favour and more than half opposed, with opposition present in every measured
social group and strongest on the right. The European Parliament's 334–324
vote to seek a Court of Justice opinion delays the politics without settling
the economics.

[? if farmers_psl_in_cabinet: PSL already carried the 2024 tractor blockade
inside this coalition. Mercosur gives it a second chance to become both the
government's agriculture minister and the government's most convincing
critic.?][? if not farmers_psl_in_cabinet: PSL has no cabinet responsibility
and can oppose the agreement without explaining the limits of Poland's vote.?]

- @mercosur_supply_chain
- @mercosur_block
- @mercosur_safeguards
- @mercosur_psl

@mercosur_supply_chain
title: Build a family-farm coalition around margins, standards and a shock fund
subtitle: Cost: 1 resource. Contest the right on material protection while preserving trade that meets enforceable labour, environmental and food standards.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: The party has no staff for a farm-income ledger and another unfunded promise will strengthen the blockade.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; rural_support += 8; labor_credibility += 5; left_poll_momentum += 0.55; psl_poll_momentum -= 0.2; konf_poll_momentum -= 0.4; pis_poll_momentum -= 0.15; eu_relations += 2; public_trust += 4; public_mood_pending_social_spending_support += 6; public_mood_pending_social_spending_left_ownership += 8; news_headline = "Family farms receive a price ledger, enforceable standards and a Mercosur shock fund"

The proposal begins with farm-gate prices, processor and supermarket margins,
then names who can trigger the safeguard investigation. A standing fund pays
small producers during the investigation instead of asking them to finance the
Union's response. Imports must meet enforceable food, labour and environmental
standards rather than a press-release promise of equivalence.

Agribusiness dislikes the distinction between its balance sheet and a family
farm. The right loses its monopoly on anger, while Lewica accepts that a trade
agreement is defensible only if the people carrying its concentrated risk can
stop it quickly and survive the stop.

- @poland_event_queue: Put the farm ledger beside the agreement

@mercosur_block
title: Join the demand to stop provisional application
subtitle: Take the majority position and the rural poll gain now, accepting a collision with the Commission and exporters who expected the agreement.
on-arrival: rural_support += 7; social_patriot_support += 5; left_poll_momentum += 0.3; konf_poll_momentum -= 0.2; psl_poll_momentum += 0.1; eu_relations -= 5; market_liberal_support -= 5; public_trust += 2; public_mood_pending_social_spending_left_ownership += 3; news_headline = "Lewica joins the Polish demand to halt Mercosur's provisional application"

Lewica treats the Court referral as a stop sign and demands that provisional
application wait. The line is popular, legible and much closer to the tractors
than a lecture on exclusive Union competence.

Exporters and Brussels answer that the interim agreement was designed to avoid
twenty-seven national vetoes. The Left has chosen who must be convinced; if the
legal challenge fails, it will own a promise no Polish minister can deliver
alone.

- @poland_event_queue: File the demand to stop application

@mercosur_safeguards
title: Defend the agreement and the five-percent safeguard trigger
subtitle: Win the European and exporter argument; hand PSL, PiS and Konfederacja a shared rural attack line.
on-arrival: eu_relations += 7; market_liberal_support += 6; foreign_policy_capacity += 3; rural_support -= 8; left_poll_momentum -= 0.4; psl_poll_momentum += 0.4; konf_poll_momentum += 0.5; pis_poll_momentum += 0.2; public_trust -= 2; news_headline = "Lewica defends Mercosur through its emergency agricultural safeguards"

The party argues that faster investigations, provisional emergency measures
and monitored quotas answer the agricultural risk without abandoning a
strategic agreement. It is a coherent European position and the one most
likely to be quoted by exporters.

At the tractor line, five percent is not a safeguard but a loss somebody must
suffer before procedure begins. Three rival parties repeat that sentence. The
agreement keeps a Polish defender and the Left discovers that trade policy can
move half a point before most voters have read its name correctly.

- @poland_event_queue: Defend the safeguard text

@mercosur_psl
title: Let PSL lead the opposition and negotiate the rural settlement
subtitle: Reduce coalition friction and give the agrarian party the largest clean polling win available in this event.
on-arrival: psl_relation += 7; psl_coalition_dissent -= 5; government_coalition_dissent -= 3 if left_in_government = 1; rural_support += 2; psl_poll_momentum += 0.7; left_poll_momentum -= 0.25; party_unity -= 1; news_headline = "PSL becomes the national address for opposition to Mercosur"

Kosiniak-Kamysz receives the microphone, the farm organisations and permission
to negotiate in the coalition's name. The arrangement is stable because every
party is doing what voters already expect it to do.

That is also its electoral effect. PSL gains a reason to exist, a government
achievement if safeguards improve and an opposition speech if they do not.
Lewica gains quieter coalition meetings and no ownership of the largest rural
argument of the year.

- @poland_event_queue: Hand PSL the negotiating file

