= 30 April 2026 — The reserve survives mainly as an invoice

Prosecutors charge three people in a second RARS investigation concerning coal
bought in 2022–23. They allege that an offer was chosen despite unmet criteria,
negative recommendations from CBA and BGK, and departures from procurement
rules. Contracts worth more than **USD 116 million** allegedly delivered coal
that did not meet the quality parameters set for the strategic reserve.

The suspects deny the charges. The allegation is not that every imported tonne
was useless or that every official joined a conspiracy; it is that officials
and suppliers allegedly converted a national energy emergency into a process
where warnings and specifications could be ignored.

[? if rars_coal_prepared = 1: The 2024 RARS ledger already records bidder,
warning, quality parameter and delivery. This sequel is damaging, but it
arrives inside the system the player chose to build.?]
[? if rars_coal_prepared = 0: Ventilators in 2020 and generators in 2024 both
offered a reusable emergency-procurement rule. Poor-quality coal is the third
invoice for declining it.?]
[? if rars_response_2024 = "RARS is Worse campaign": The parody collection
has found a winter line. The institutional answer remains out of stock.?]

- @rars_coal_ledger
- @rars_coal_case
- @rars_coal_mountain

