= 10 June 2026 — One dirty line contaminates the whole bundle

The funds ministry says it cannot certify Czyste Powietrze expenditure after
finding cases where spending covered by individual investigations had not been
excluded. The immediate exposure is wider than insulation and heat pumps: the
reimbursement package totals **PLN 3.5 billion** and also contains roads, rail,
metro, water infrastructure and primary-health projects.

EPPO reports a systemic investigation into possible failures by officials at
the environmental fund and climate ministry in designing and implementing
stages of the programme from January 2022 to February 2026. The inquiry is
developing. Questioned expenditure is not yet a final loss, and an
investigation is not proof that every installer, household or programme stage
was corrupt.

[? if clean_air_audit_prepared = 1: HoReCa taught the player to freeze risk,
not an entire programme, and climate capacity kept enough people to apply the
lesson. The coalition still owns the failure but not a blind response.?]
[? if clean_air_audit_prepared = 0: The KPO controls were treated as a yacht
story or a one-off correction. The same missing beneficiary-and-invoice trail
can now delay transport and health reimbursements too.?]
[? if left_in_government = 1: Lewica cannot campaign as though the climate
ministry is a foreign country. Our cabinet must separate household delivery
from the expenditure it cannot certify.?][? if left_in_government = 0: From
opposition, we can force publication without becoming the authority that signs
the European claim.?]

- @clean_air_quarantine
- @clean_air_register
- @clean_air_blame

@clean_air_quarantine
title: Quarantine every flagged invoice and submit only the clean package
subtitle: Government route. Prior HoReCa controls make the separation faster; without them, delivery and reimbursement both slow.
view-if: left_in_government = 1
on-arrival: {!
Q.clean_air_response_2026 = "Invoice quarantine";
Q.kpo_scrutiny += 8;
Q.kpo_delivery += Q.clean_air_audit_prepared ? 2 : -2;
Q.kpo_public_credit += Q.clean_air_audit_prepared ? 5 : 2;
Q.climate_state_capacity += Q.clean_air_audit_prepared ? 3 : 1;
Q.eu_relations += 5;
Q.public_trust += 7;
Q.institutional_trust += 5;
Q.left_poll_momentum += Q.clean_air_audit_prepared ? 0.45 : 0.1;
Q.public_mood_pending_social_spending_left_ownership += 7;
Q.news_headline =
    "Flagged clean-air invoices leave the EU claim before the clean package is signed";
!}

Each investigated invoice is removed with a case number; the remainder is
certified without pretending that a ministry assurance can substitute for the
documents. Households whose work is compliant remain in the programme.

Earlier risk controls turn this into a filter. Without them, officials build
the filter while the PLN 3.5 billion package waits.

- @poland_event_queue: Submit the clean file

